WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.500
- It has been, is it 20 years?

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:02.730
That you and your wife have been together?

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:03.563
- Something like that.

00:00:03.563 --> 00:00:04.396
A long time.
- That's crazy.

00:00:04.396 --> 00:00:05.640
(audience applauding and cheering)

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:06.690
Congratulations!

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:07.523
- [Jake] Thank you.

00:00:07.523 --> 00:00:08.607
- That's hard to do.

00:00:08.607 --> 00:00:09.630
But so wait-

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:12.000
- The beautiful Erin Payne made it up!

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.290
- When did y'all meet?

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:14.460
- So when I first moved to LA

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:16.590
she was a bartender at
The Cat and The Fiddle.

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:17.423
- Okay.

00:00:17.423 --> 00:00:18.256
- And when I-

00:00:18.256 --> 00:00:19.089
- Oh, I like The Cat and the Fiddle.

00:00:19.089 --> 00:00:19.922
- It was a great place.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:19.922 --> 00:00:20.755
- The original one too on Sunset.

00:00:20.755 --> 00:00:22.260
And when I saw her I had that like moment

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.080
where I was like, "Oh
wow, like there she is!"

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:25.913
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:25.913 --> 00:00:27.224
- And she did not have the same moment.

00:00:27.224 --> 00:00:29.100
(everyone laughing)

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.210
And you know very quickly

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.400
when somebody's not feeling it back.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.057
So I had like a, "Hey, what are you doing?

00:00:34.057 --> 00:00:34.890
"How are you?"

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:36.870
And she's like, "What do
you want from the bar?"

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:37.703
- [Kelly] Yeah.
(audience laughing)

00:00:37.703 --> 00:00:40.320
- And so I started going to all her shifts

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.060
and I would just drink coffee.
- Oh my god.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:42.893
- [Jake] And hang out.

00:00:42.893 --> 00:00:43.980
- Some people call that stalking.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.450
- Yeah, I stalked her.
(everyone laughing)

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:46.350
- I was like-
- 100%.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:47.183
- I love that, okay.

00:00:47.183 --> 00:00:48.186
- And so I went there, I hung out-

00:00:48.186 --> 00:00:49.470
- And you went and got coffee?

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:51.000
- Yeah, because-
- At a bar?

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.178
- Well, it was an afternoon.

00:00:52.178 --> 00:00:53.640
- Oh, okay.
- So she was a day bartender.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:56.100
- You would've been frowned
upon to have maybe a vodka.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.020
- Yeah, well also it's not
gonna work if I'm hitting on her

00:00:58.020 --> 00:00:58.980
if I'm like a drunk.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:00.030
- Yeah, that's true.
(audience laughing)

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:00.863
That's true.

00:01:00.863 --> 00:01:01.696
This is a good thing.

00:01:01.696 --> 00:01:03.120
- Yeah, so I sat there for all her shifts.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:04.890
She did not notice me.
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:06.990
She didn't notice I was there.
- This is the best story.

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:08.640
- And then after about
two and a half months,

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:10.800
I finally had a moment where we talked.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.345
And I had heard everything
she had said to other people.

00:01:13.345 --> 00:01:14.178
- [Kelly] Oh!

00:01:14.178 --> 00:01:15.870
- So I could connect on everything.

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:18.195
- This is totally stalking. (laughs)

00:01:18.195 --> 00:01:19.440
(audience laughing)

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:20.490
Like your first date,

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:21.323
you were like,

00:01:21.323 --> 00:01:22.156
you knew all this information.

00:01:22.156 --> 00:01:23.220
- Not even the date. At the bar.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:24.090
She's like, "How you doing?"

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:26.310
I'm like, "I've just
been training for a 5 K."

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:28.050
She's like, "I'm training for a 10 K."

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:30.101
I'm like, "What?"
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:01:30.101 --> 00:01:31.770
And then she's-
- That's crazy!

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:33.937
- I was like, "Yeah, I'm just
thinking about getting a dog.

00:01:33.937 --> 00:01:34.980
"I love rescue dogs."

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:36.810
She's like, "I have a rescue dog."

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:37.854
I'm like-
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:01:37.854 --> 00:01:39.293
This is insane!

00:01:39.293 --> 00:01:41.223
We should get outta here.
- Oh my god!

00:01:41.223 --> 00:01:42.763
We should get married!

00:01:42.763 --> 00:01:44.430
- We should get married!
(audience applauding)

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:45.263
- I love that though!

00:01:45.263 --> 00:01:46.890
That you knew what you wanted.

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:47.789
- Yeah.
- And you went for it.

00:01:47.789 --> 00:01:49.830
- Yeah.
- That's awesome.

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:51.023
And 20 years, that's incredible.

00:01:51.023 --> 00:01:51.916
(audience cheering)

00:01:51.916 --> 00:01:52.953
Later that day,

00:01:52.953 --> 00:01:56.700
the very funny Natasha Leggero
joined the conversation

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:58.140
and she was quick to reveal

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:00.693
the biggest ways her life
changed in the pandemic.

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:02.700
So you're normally that,

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:03.533
just kind of-

00:02:03.533 --> 00:02:04.470
- Well, I'm just like-
- Just shove it.

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:06.180
- I just started to get frustrated

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:07.013
'cause I'm like, you know-

00:02:07.013 --> 00:02:08.220
- 'Cause everything's filtered.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:10.020
- Yes, and then during the pandemic,

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:11.730
I just couldn't keep up, you know.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.050
It's like-

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:14.370
- Isn't the pandemic the time

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:15.840
that you would have all
the time in the world

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:17.490
to clean your closet? (laughs)

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:18.763
- Well, here's the thing.

00:02:18.763 --> 00:02:20.490
(Kelly claps)

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:21.690
Here's my philosophy,

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:23.400
like husbands in the pandemic,

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:24.233
like look, Jake,

00:02:24.233 --> 00:02:25.560
they all have these annoying hobbies.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:27.735
Like Jake is now an amateur carpenter.

00:02:27.735 --> 00:02:29.100
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.950
My husband is like, he became a DJ.

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:34.500
A techno DJ in the pandemic.
- Wait, what?

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:35.333
- Horrifying.

00:02:35.333 --> 00:02:37.650
My other friend is like
crocheting baseball caps.

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:39.150
- Is it horrifying?
(Jake laughing)

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:41.070
- Do you know what women
did in the pandemic?

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:41.970
Mothers?

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:43.319
They did laundry.
(Jake and audience laughing)

00:02:43.319 --> 00:02:45.450
- And cooked like every meal.

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:47.070
- I know!
- Like every, yes.

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:48.090
And I was done.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:49.247
- I'm over male hobbies, sorry Jake.

00:02:49.247 --> 00:02:51.090
- Make a sandwich.
- Okay, I get it.

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:51.990
Look, I get it, I get it.

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:54.540
- I love that he became a techno DJ.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:55.377
- Well then, you marry him.

00:02:55.377 --> 00:02:56.940
- No, no, no!

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:59.310
When I say I love, I mean that is weird.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:00.445
A weird thing.
- Well-

00:03:00.445 --> 00:03:01.530
He already did it.
- Oh!

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:04.983
- And then he tried to reprise
it from like, 20 years ago.

00:03:04.983 --> 00:03:06.390
- (laughs) Glory Days.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:08.258
It's like Glory Days!

00:03:08.258 --> 00:03:09.653
This is amazing!

00:03:09.653 --> 00:03:12.600
There's a show in this. (laughs)

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:13.433
I love that.

00:03:13.433 --> 00:03:16.020
So wait, you seem to collect toothbrushes.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:18.510
So we just stalk you online.

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:20.108
- [Natasha] Okay, that is so embarrassing.

00:03:20.108 --> 00:03:20.941
(Jake laughing)

00:03:20.941 --> 00:03:23.062
- [Kelly] How many people
live at your house? (laughs)

00:03:23.062 --> 00:03:24.030
My god.

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:26.040
- I do not collect toothbrushes.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:27.758
But okay, so I have a-
- You do.

00:03:27.758 --> 00:03:30.330
- (laughs) I have a, oh, that close up.

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:32.460
Okay, I have a podcast with my husband.

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:33.900
It's called The Endless Honeymoon Podcast.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:36.630
And now I've decided instead
of getting couples therapy,

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:39.420
I just ambush him with my
issues during the taping.

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:40.260
- I love y'all.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:41.403
- And-
- Okay.

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:45.750
- The last issue we had was
that he just uses my toothbrush.

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:47.670
And I'm like, "That is not okay."

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:48.503
- That is-
- He's like, "What?

00:03:48.503 --> 00:03:49.336
"We're married."

00:03:49.336 --> 00:03:50.400
So I brought it to the podcast.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:52.230
- How does that translate?

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:53.063
What?

00:03:53.063 --> 00:03:53.970
We're married so I can
use your toothbrush.

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:54.870
- I don't know.
(audience laughing)

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:56.280
He's just like-

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:57.113
Would you do that?

00:03:57.113 --> 00:03:59.040
- Yes.
(audience laughing)

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:00.240
You're married!

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.440
- [Natasha] See what I mean?

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:02.340
It's disgusting.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:06.180
- You don't lick someone's
like plaque on their teeth.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:07.350
Like I just like, wait, what?

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:08.183
When you-

00:04:08.183 --> 00:04:09.630
- Well, you rinse the
toothbrush afterwards.

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:11.160
It always starts clean!

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:12.450
- Yes, but god.

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:14.400
I feel like it's a very
dirty part of your mouth.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:15.660
I'm so not into that.
- It's disgusting.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:17.040
- What is this? A man thing?

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:17.873
- I don't know.

00:04:17.873 --> 00:04:19.140
Well, 100% of the people-

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:20.550
You didn't chime in on my Instagram,

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:21.960
but everybody,

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:23.820
they shamed my husband so hard

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:25.909
that he went out and
bought 40 toothbrushes.

00:04:25.909 --> 00:04:26.910
(everyone laughing)
(Kelly clapping)

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.560
And now I can't even find mine.

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:29.813
He's just like-
- Like lost in the abyss.

00:04:29.813 --> 00:04:31.440
- He just got them everywhere.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:32.880
But there is nothing worse

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:34.650
than going to grab like your toothbrush

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:36.330
and it's soaking wet.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.740
So disgusting.

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:38.573
- Oh, it's intimate.

00:04:38.573 --> 00:04:39.406
- [Kelly] No, no.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:42.810
- Maybe the first three months of dating.

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:43.643
- Agreed, agreed.

00:04:43.643 --> 00:04:44.476
It changes, it's a little gross.

00:04:44.476 --> 00:04:46.020
- When you're still lying.

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:47.910
And you're like, "Yeah,
I'm totally into that."

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:49.680
And you're not.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:50.880
That's the grossest thing ever.

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:52.380
It happened to me one time with my kid.

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:54.600
My kid used mine and didn't
know that you couldn't.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:55.433
And I was like-

00:04:55.433 --> 00:04:56.670
I don't even drink after people.

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:57.840
Like I don't like,

00:04:57.840 --> 00:04:58.950
that's just gross.

00:04:58.950 --> 00:04:59.916
Like people's saliva,

00:04:59.916 --> 00:05:00.845
I'm just like (retches).

00:05:00.845 --> 00:05:01.678
- Yeah.

00:05:01.678 --> 00:05:03.386
- And when you put that wet
toothbrush in your mouth.

00:05:03.386 --> 00:05:05.550
- Ugh.

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:06.750
- I literally almost vomited.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:08.490
It was the grossest thing ever.

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:09.720
And it's my own child.

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:11.751
Sorry, River.
- Sorry, River. (laughs)

00:05:11.751 --> 00:05:12.584
- Yeah, sorry,

00:05:12.584 --> 00:05:14.702
but I don't want your nasty
mouth on my toothbrush.

00:05:14.702 --> 00:05:16.710
Like especially a child.

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:18.440
They never brush their teeth.
- I know!

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:20.400
- They lie to you about it.
- I know.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.900
- And then it's like how
much plaque was on there?

